{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/764431-one-on-one-games","id":764431,"title":"One-On-One Games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-12T15:14:22-08:00","id":764431,"title":"One-On-One Games","content":"Like the topic says - what would, in your opinion, be the best setting for a one-on-one game? I know roleplaying in general works much better in groups, but I have to work with what I've got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5128-synderryn","name":"Synderryn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:12:49-08:00","id":764476,"title":"","content":"Any game can be one on one, it just depends on how much work you the St want to put into world and npc building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:08:44-08:00","id":764531,"title":"","content":"What you and your player are most keen on is probably the most useful answer, but to generalise:<br /> <br /> One-on-one games can be scaled-down versions of regular games with or without NPC allies forming a &quot;party&quot; around the player's character or the player controlling more than one, but they often use the solo nature to emphasise the isolation and vulnerability of the central character, or their power and versatility. (For examples from other games, there are solo <b>Call Of Cthulhu</b> adventures built heavily around isolation and there are also one-on-one rules for playing elite spies in <b>James Bond 007</b> while groups are advised to play rookie agents.) It's also a chance play that loner or &quot;special snowflake&quot; character who wouldn't fit a group game.<br /> <br /> Mortals, vampires and wraiths are well suited to horror games about one character alone and possibly vulnerable in an uncaring or hostile world. Mages have an advantage of versatility in their use of power and are suited to games about powerful solo protagonists. Werewolves and Changelings have a stronger social structure, but still have room for loners - the cancelled computer game <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Werewolf:_The_Apocalypse_-_The_Heart_of_Gaia\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Apocalypse - The Heart Of Gaia</a> featured a &quot;lost cub&quot; as the player's character. Hunters and Demons are both &quot;new arrivals&quot; to the classic <b>World Of Darkness</b> with little support and little reason to trust others, so they could suit solo games as well - <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b> developer and <b>Demon: The Descent</b> creator Rose Bailey posted Actual Play reports of <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?78045-Actual-Play-Demon-Strange-As-Angels\" target=\"_blank\">a Demon: The Fallen game</a> using a system hack in 2003, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:37:08-08:00","id":764559,"title":"","content":"I've done Vampire and Wraith as solo games before. Both worked well. But it can be taxing on both parties.<br /> <br /> The idea of one player running a troupe of characters might also work. Lifting the model off Ars Magica somewhat, you could create a vampire/ghost/mage/changeling, and then build around them a cast of ghouls/fetters/familiars/chimerical companions. The ST can play these for the most part, but when the protagonist goes into slumber or torpor or a seeking, or goes off to find Transcendence/Ascension/Golconda, etc, the player can play one of the other characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T04:48:42-08:00","id":764850,"title":"","content":"Me and a friend of mine primarily run one-on-one's and have several games going between each other including Vampire the Masquerade, Demon the Fallen, Mage the Awakening and Princess the Hopeful. We run a very mix-matchy version of WoD which mixes a lot of things between old and new, but sufficed to say when we play we're doing perfectly dandy and focus mainly on the golden rule of &quot;Have fun&quot; before anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T10:40:31-08:00","id":765038,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, guys. I guess now I just need to figure out what type of storyline would be best suited for one-on-one. It's just myself and my husband - we haven't decided yet between the two of us who is going to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5128-synderryn","name":"Synderryn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T10:32:00-08:00","id":765642,"title":"","content":"Do either of you have an innate preference for being either a player or storyteller? I also think at least VtM have a book or two on single-player games. Alien Hunger I think it might've been? Don't know about nWoD, maybe google has more answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T11:36:11-08:00","id":765682,"title":"","content":"funny enough. i always thought Promethean was Meant to be played alone<br /> <br /> <br /> Wraith ban be a fun experience (specially if you go a la Crow on Risen). and Hunter the Reckoning can be particularly interesting playing alone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T17:38:33-08:00","id":765909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/764431-one-on-one-games?p=765642#post765642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think at least VtM have a book or two on single-player games. Alien Hunger I think it might've been?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Alien Hunger</b> is a quickstart adventure designed with five pregenerated player characters. (It could be adapted to fewer, but that goes for most published adventures.)<br /> <br /> There's a section on troupe-style play and advice that might be useful for solo games in the revised <b>Players Guide</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T22:49:15-08:00","id":766074,"title":"","content":"Righto, I stand corrected; hope it's helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}